{"id": "section-body-03988", "title": "Zika Virus Disease", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Viral Infections", "Zika Virus Disease"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03988", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Zika Virus Disease", "runs": [{"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disease"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03989", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Zika virus is a flavivirus that is transmitted primarily through the bite of an infected mosquito, primarily Aedes aegypti, and also Aedes albopictus, the same mosquitoes that transmit dengue, chikungunya, and yellow fever. Zika virus can also be transmitted in-utero from mother to fetus, and through sexual contact, blood transfusion, and organ transplantation. Zika virus infections are usually asymptomatic. When symptoms occur, they tend to be mild and include mild fever, rash, conjunctivitis, and muscle and joint pain that last for 2 to 7 days. There is no specific treatment but symptoms can be treated with common fever medicines, rest and drinking fluids.", "runs": [{"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "flavivirus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transmitted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primarily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "through"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bite"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mosquito,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primarily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Aedes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aegypti,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also Aedes albopictus, the same mosquitoes that transmit dengue, chikungunya, and yellow fever. Zika virus can also be transmitted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in-utero"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mother"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fetus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "through"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contact,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transfusion,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "organ"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transplantation."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus infections are usually asymptomatic. When symptoms occur, they tend to be mild and include mild fever, rash, conjunctivitis, and muscle and joint pain that last for 2 to 7 days."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "There is no specific treatment but symptoms can be treated with common fever medicines, rest and drinking fluids."}]}, {"id": "body-03991", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definition", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definition"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03993", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Suspected Case: Any person presenting with rash and/or fever and at least one of the following signs or symptoms:", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presenting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rash"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and/or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "one"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "following"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms:"}]}, {"id": "body-03994", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "arthralgia; or", "runs": [{"text": "arthralgia;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1775"}}, {"id": "body-03995", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "arthritis; or", "runs": [{"text": "arthritis;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1775"}}, {"id": "body-03996", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "conjunctivitis (non-purulent/hyperaemic).", "runs": [{"text": "conjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(non-purulent/hyperaemic)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1775"}}, {"id": "body-03998", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Probable case: A suspected case with presence of IgM antibody against Zika virus and an epidemiological link (with no evidence of infection with other flaviviruses).", "runs": [{"text": "Probable", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "case: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "A suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "IgM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibody"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "against"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epidemiological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "link"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "no evidence of infection with other flaviviruses)."}]}, {"id": "body-04000", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Confirmed case: Any person with laboratory confirmation of recent Zika virus infection presence of Zika virus RNA or antigen in serum or other samples (e.g., saliva, urine, tissue, whole blood); or IgM antibody against Zika virus positive and Plague Reduction Neutralizing Test (PRNT90) for Zika virus with titre ≥20 and Zika virus PRNT90 titre ratio ≥ 4 compared to other flaviviruses; and exclusion of other flaviviruses.", "runs": [{"text": "Confirmed", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Zika"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "RNA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antigen in serum or other samples (e.g., saliva, urine, tissue, whole blood); or IgM antibody against Zika virus positive and Plague Reduction Neutralizing Test (PRNT90) for Zika virus with titre ≥20 and Zika virus PRNT90 titre ratio ≥ 4 compared to other flaviviruses; and exclusion of other flaviviruses."}]}, {"id": "body-04002", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Diagnostic Criteria:", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Criteria:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Fever, skin rashes, conjunctivitis,", "runs": [{"text": "Fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rashes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conjunctivitis,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1775"}}, {"id": "body-04004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Joint pain, malaise, Headache - usually mild and last for 2–7 days.", "runs": [{"text": "Joint"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malaise,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Headache"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {